WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:01.609
Speaker 1: Matt Gates.

00:00:01.609 --> 00:00:08.540
It's almost like every day there's a new scandal
facing beleaguered Republican Congressman

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.580
Matt Gates.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:15.310
Earlier this week, we told you about his apparent
involvement in running a shill candidate in

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:16.740
Florida's 9th District.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.710
I won't retell the entire story, but you can
check it out on our YouTube channel or the

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.119
podcast from earlier this week.

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:26.329
I think it was Monday or Tuesday where we
covered that.

00:00:26.329 --> 00:00:31.779
We also know that he is being looked at for
involvement in child sex trafficking and a

00:00:31.779 --> 00:00:32.929
whole bunch of other things.

00:00:32.929 --> 00:00:37.710
The FBI or federal authorities, rather, seized
his iPhone some time ago.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.989
It's looking really, really bad for Matt Gates.

00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:46.809
Republican Congressman Steve Scalise, who
is a horrible person, says that.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:55.730
Indeed, Matt Gates is charged, if there are
charges levied against him, that they would

00:00:55.730 --> 00:01:02.819
take action and remove him from his committee
assignments if the Department of Justice files

00:01:02.819 --> 00:01:08.820
charges, according to Newsweek, Scarless added
that historically, lawmakers who face charges

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.390
have been removed from committee assignments
immediately as a precedent.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:14.420
This is the same.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:21.750
This mirrors the House Republican rules that
lawmakers indicted for felonies and sentenced

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.780
to at least two years in prison must resign.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.270
Now, the weird thing about sentenced to two
years in prison is their terms are only two

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.280
years long.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:35.840
So that sort of seems a little strange that
you have to resign from committees.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.400
But I guess you could be sentenced and get
a suspended sentence or something like that.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.400
I don't know.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.740
Scarless going on to say it's hard to speculate
on rumors, but if something really formal

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.259
happened from justice, we would, of course,
react and take action.

00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:52.369
Scarless says he has not spoken with Matt
Gates and has not heard Matt Gates's explanation

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:57.689
for the allegations, but imagines he will
be speaking with him this week, saying, quote,

00:01:57.689 --> 00:01:59.560
It's serious things alleged.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.870
Obviously, we will want to get the facts.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:11.090
Gates continues to deny the allegations, although
the denials often also include raising the

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.760
alarm with additional derogatory information.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:21.190
For example, when he first went on Tucker
Carlson's show to deny some element of the

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:22.190
allegations.

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:26.190
He also said, I've never paid anyone for sex,
which at the time was not even part of what

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.700
we thought was going on.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.880
Increasingly, it seems Matt Gates actually
has paid people for sex.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.630
And whatever your thoughts are about paying
people for sex, the bone headedness of Matt

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:40.690
Gates raising new issues that weren't even
yet being looked at.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:43.240
It's odd to say the least.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.490
Gates did not go to a weekly meeting of House
Republicans yesterday, according to Steve

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:50.270
Scalise.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:55.340
And it seems as though increasingly many Republicans
I mean, like it seems like Marjorie Taylor

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:56.810
Greene is sort of sticking with them.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:59.340
She may go down with the ship.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:05.190
It seems as though, you know, some of the
wackier members are sticking with Matt Gates,

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.460
but increasingly lots of people are abandoning
him.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.040
It may indeed be a ship that simply goes down.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.150
Now, as far as judiciary, there's a kind of
weird I don't know if I'd call it.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:22.650
I guess it is a conflict of interest because
Matt Gates is currently on the Judiciary Committee.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:28.920
The House Judiciary Committee has oversight
power over the very Department of Justice

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.730
that would be indicting Matt Gates.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:37.100
It's not as though there's a very clear way
in which he's going to be able to do X or

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.830
Y as it relates to the investigation against
them.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:44.920
But Steve Scalise saying, well, he'll he'll
have to resign from the committees if there

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.300
are charges.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:51.820
And one of the committees he's on does oversight
of the entity that would be charging him.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:55.170
That's you know, that that that's certainly
a question mark.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:59.710
And then lastly, you know, Steve Scalise,
as I mentioned, is or is a horrible person.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.310
He really can't be trusted.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:03.800
So there's a question of whether they will
actually do it.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.560
It's clearly in the House rules.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:11.840
Scalise is saying Republicans would demand
that he do it.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.570
I wouldn't be shocked if Gates does get charged.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:19.930
And the House, controlled by Democrats based
on the rules, moves forward with stripping

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.870
Gates of his committee assignments.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:27.070
I wouldn't be shocked if some Republicans
pulled out the allegations alone or not evidence.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.020
And this isn't what should happen, even though
these are the House rules.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.820
We'll wait and see.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:36.150
I'm increasingly of the mindset that there's
probably some kind of charge coming against

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:42.139
Matt Gates, but without a doubt, he is innocent
until proven guilty and he is not yet even

00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:43.139
been charged.

00:04:43.139 --> 00:04:45.629
So we have to allow the investigations to
be carried out

